1. The libraries that go into the programs you make: MIT License

     crates/phai-ui     crates/phai-data    crates/phai-web
     crates/phai-pack   apps/setup (the setup program Publish makes)
     and the examples:  apps/sample, apps/gallery, docs/help-src/examples

   Use them in any program, free or sold, without asking.
   The text is in LICENSES/MIT.txt and in each of those folders.

2. Phai Studio itself: PolyForm Perimeter License 1.0.1

     everything else: apps/studio, crates/phai-editor, crates/phai-form,
     crates/phai-design, crates/phai-debug, the guide and the website

   Use it, change it and share it for any purpose, making programs you sell
   included, but not to offer others a product that competes with Phai Studio
   (a copy or a changed version under another name, for example).
   The text is in LICENSES/PolyForm-Perimeter-1.0.1.md.

